      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To observe the changes of plasma von Willebrand factor (vWF) and soluble E-selectin (sE-selectin) in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD) and evaluate their clinic significance."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The level of plasma vWF and sE-selectin of 60 cases with coronary artery disease were detected by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) and 20 healthy persons acted as the control group. Risk factors for coronary artery disease were obtained by asking the medical history and the relation ship was analyzed with coronary artery disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The plasma vWF and sE-selectin levels of CAD patients were significantly higher than those of the control group (P = 0.017 and P < 0.001). There was no significant difference in plasma vWF levels between the acute myocardial infarction (AMI) group and the unstable angina pectoris (UA) group or the SA group (P = 0.210 and P = 0.194). The plasma vWF level of the SA group were higher than that of the UA group (P = 0.012). The plasma levels of sE-selectin of AMI group, and the UA group were higher than those of the SA group (P < 0.001 and P = 0.010). There were no significant differences between the SA group and the control group (P = 0.284) and between the AMI group and the UA group (P = 0.066)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The increased plasma vWF or sE-selectin level may be risk factors for CAD and they may be involved in the pathogenesis of CAD. The increase of plasma sE-selectin is correlated to the generation and development of CAD and it is important in the evaluation of clinical severity of CAD."
        }
      ]},
